[ti:Week03-Mon.mp3]

[00:00.00]expense 熟义 n. 费用；开销；[pl.] 花费；业务费用 示例 ① While company managers have known about the benefits for a long time, many have done little about it, sceptical of whether they could trust their employees to work to full capacity without supervision, or concerned about the additional expenses teleworking policies might incur as staff start charging their home phone bills to the business. 尽管公司经理们早已获知这些好处，但许多人却很少付诸行动。他们怀疑能否信任他们的雇员在没有监管的情况下还能全力工作，或者担心在家办公政策所产生的额外费用，如员工可能会把家里的电话账单充作公务通信的费用。（2009. 12）② They were supposed to buy safety equipment at their own expense. 他们本应该自费购买安全设备。
[00:13.10]somewhat 熟义 ad. 有点，有些，稍微 示例 ① Defending champion Anand is becoming somewhat long in the tooth and has won only one major tournament since his successful title defence in Moscow a year ago. 卫冕冠军阿南德年纪有点大了，自从他一年前在莫斯科成功卫冕之后只赢过一次重大比赛。（The Guardian） ② He finally agreed, somewhat reluctantly, to go shopping with me. 他最终还是勉强答应陪我一起去购物。
[00:20.52]accuse 熟义 vt. 控告，控诉，谴责 示例 ① A regional official says a notorious militia leader accused of enlisting child soldiers for cross-border raids from Liberia into western Ivory Coast was killed during fighting Saturday. 当地的一位官员说一个臭名昭著的民兵头子在周六的战斗中被打死了，他曾被指控征募童兵从利比里亚进入到西象牙海岸从事跨境突袭活动。（The Washington Post） ② He claims that his boss accused him of theft. 他声称老板告他偷窃。
[00:28.68]millimetre 熟义 n. 毫米 示例 ① Two prototype antennas for the world's largest array of millimetre-wave telescopes have passed a key test, working together to track and image Saturn for more than an hour on 2 March, 2007. 为世界上最大的毫米波望远镜阵列配备的两个样品天线已经通过一项重要测试 ——在2007年3月2日协同工作，跟踪并为土星拍照一个多小时。（New Scientist） ② My math teacher tells me that there are 1,000 millimetres in a meter. 我的数学老师告诉我一米等于1000毫米。
[00:37.47]elsewhere 熟义 ad. 在(或去、到)别处 示例 ① A well-known study examined students who got into highly selective schools and then went elsewhere. 一项著名的研究调查了那些本已进入精英学校后来又去了其他学校的学生。（2008. 6） ② The book is sold out here and you'll have to go elsewhere to buy it. 这书卖完了，你得到别处去买了。 语料 It is not easy to find happiness in ourselves, and it is not possible to find it elsewhere. 要从我们自身找到幸福是不容易的，而要从别的地方找到幸福则是不可能的。（美国女散文家雷普利尔）
[00:46.52]litre 熟义 n. 升(容量单位) 示例 ① Finally, while no fault of Bloomberg's, nothing in his proposal gets at one of the roots of Americans' over-consumption of soda—that is, the wrong-headed agricultural subsidies that have resulted in a litre bottle of Coke being cheaper than a similar-sized container of skim milk. 尽管这并不是布隆伯格的错，但最终他的任何提议都没有触及美国过度消耗苏打水的根源，也就是说，是判断错误的农业补贴导致了一升瓶装可乐要比同体积脱脂牛奶便宜。（The Guardian） ② This new car is equipped with a 2-litre gasoline engine. 这辆新车配备了排量为2升的汽油发动机。
[00:57.36]host 熟义 n. 主人；东道主；节目主持人 ‖ v. 主办；主持（电视或广播节目等）；做东 示例 ① Their breakthrough, simply put, was that when their search engine crawled the Web, it did more than just looks for word matches; it also tallied and ranked a host of other critical factors like how websites link to one another. 简单来说，他们的突破发生在搜索引擎在网络上慢慢传播的时候，引擎提供的不仅仅是找寻匹配的词语，还可以根据一些关键指标如网页如何相连对主页进行统计和排序。（2007. 6）② The college is playing host to a group of visiting American scientists. 学院正在接待一批来访的美国科学家。
[01:07.70]ward 熟义 n. 病房；选区；受监护人 ‖v. 防止，避免 示例 ① Embedded in the floor are heating elements intended to ward off the cold weather and keep winter-weary feet cozy. 嵌入地板内的发热元件是为了抵御寒冷的天气，使饱受冬季折磨的双脚感到舒适。（The Washington Post） ② She carried a knife to ward off attacks. 她带了一把刀自卫，以抵挡攻击。
[01:13.70]highly 熟义 ad. 很，非常；高度地；赞赏地 示例 ① According to the college, the plan is designed for high-ability, highly motivated students who wish to save money or to move along more rapidly toward advanced degrees. 据校方称，这一方案就是为那些能力强、学习积极性非常高且希望省钱或者更快攻读高级学位的学生设计的。（2012. 6）② Everyone we talked to spoke very highly of her. 与我们谈话的每个人都对她大加称赞。
[01:21.09]luxury 熟义 n. 奢侈，奢华；奢侈品 示例 ① The company behind Gucci and Yves Saint Laurent has been selling off its retail operations in recent years to focus more on its luxury brands. 位列古琦和伊夫圣罗兰之后的这家公司近些年一直在廉价出清其零售业务，将更多精力集中到奢侈品牌。（The Washington Post） ② She allows herself the luxury of a sauna once a week in the summer. 夏日里，她让自己每周享受一次桑拿浴。
[01:28.41]display 熟义 vt. 陈列；显露 ‖n. 陈列；表演；表露 示例 ① Google will be able to display up to 20% of orphan works for free, include them in its subscription deals to libraries and sell them to individual buyers under the consumer licence. 谷歌将能免费展示多达20%的无主作品，并将这些作品包含在与图书馆订立的订阅协议中或按照消费许可出售给个体购买者。（2011. 12）② He displayed his bruises for all to see. 他将自己身上青一块紫一块的伤痕露出来给大家看。
[01:36.38]acute 熟义 a. 十分严重的；(疾病)急性的；(感官)灵敏的；敏锐的 示例 ① To be sure, many social-media users have an acute sense of skepticism. 的确，许多社会媒体使用者有敏锐的怀疑意识。（Newsweek） ② There is an acute shortage of water in the northwestern area of China. 中国的西北地区严重缺水。
[01:41.59]reserve 熟义 vt. 预订；保留；保留做某事的权利‖ n. 储备，贮藏(物) 示例 ① Indeed, we didn't hear about "men's language" until people began to respond to girls' appropriation of forms normally reserved for boys and men. 事实上，直到人们对女孩子借用一般留给男孩子和男人使用的语言形式（这种现象）开始回应之后我们才听说“男性语言”。（2007. 6） ② I've reserved a room in the name of Tom. 我以汤姆的名字预订了一个房间。
[01:48.77]precede 熟义 vt. 在…之前发生(或出现)；走在…前面 示例 ① The historical aspect of the Blair era matters because it has become fashionable to treat it merely as a continuum from the Thatcher era which preceded it. 从历史的角度看，布莱尔时代很重要，因为人们已经普遍认为其与之前的撒切尔时代是连续统一体。（The Guardian）② His English teacher preceded him out of the classroom. 他的英语老师先于他走出了教室。
[01:56.14]prominent 熟义 a. 重要的；显著的；突出的 示例 ① Many will have heard of the most prominent names from that tradition: Theodor Adorno, Herbert Marcuse and Max Horkheimer, but its reach goes much further, taking in many of the 20th century's most important continental philosophers and socio-political developments. 很多人都听说过在那一传统下最著名的人物：西奥多•阿多诺、赫伯特• 马库塞和马克斯•霍克海默，但如果将许多20 世纪最重要的大陆哲学家和社会政治发展贡献者包括在内，将有更多的人位列其中。（The Guardian） ② He played a prominent part in the movement of environment protection. 他在环保运动中发挥了重要作用。
[02:07.50]consequently 熟义 ad. 因此，所以 示例 ① Babies, in case you hadn't noticed, are the polar opposite of adults, and consequently they exist in a state of almost constant amazement at everything. 可能你没有注意到，婴儿与成年人是截然相反的，因此他们总是对任何事情都感到惊奇。（The Guardian） ② We've increased the number of staff and consequently the service is better. 我们增加了人手，因此服务质量更好了。
[02:15.08]phase 熟义 n. 阶段，时期 ‖ v. 分阶段进行，逐步做 示例 ① That announcement caused panic in markets, helping to push Ireland and Portugal over the brink and initiating a second, more dangerous, phase of the euro crisis. 这个公告造成了市场恐慌，将爱尔兰和葡萄牙推到了悬崖边缘，并引发了第二轮更危险的欧元危机。（The Economist） ② Her anxiety about the future was just a passing phase. 她对未来的担心只是暂时的。
[02:22.50]cultivate 熟义 v. 耕作；培养，养成 示例 ① What are your aims? We're looking to cultivate an appreciation and a love of science. 你们的目标是什么？我们期望培养（人们）对科学的欣赏与热爱。（New Scientist） ② Most of the world's fertile land has already been cultivated. 世界上绝大多数肥沃土地都已经被开垦过了。
[02:28.05]deliberate 熟义 a. 故意的；深思熟虑的；从容的 示例 ① Every time any official in Beijing deliberates publicly about seeking an alternative to the U.S. dollar for the $2.1 trillion China holds in reserve, currency traders have a heart attack. 每次任何一位北京的官员公开讨论寻找另外一种货币替代美元作为中国现在持有的2.1万亿美元的外汇储备时，外汇交易商们都会紧张得心脏病发作。（2012. 12）② I'm sure the omission of his name was deliberate. 我确信他不写名字是有意而为。
[02:36.47]preach 熟义 v. 布道；宣扬；说教 示例 ① Barry's prolific historical paintings demonstrate his ambition to rival the painters of antiquity and the Renaissance and to practise what the then president of the RA, Sir Joshua Reynolds, always preached—that history painting was the noblest form of art. 巴里的众多历史性画作都表明他渴望与古代以及文艺复兴时期的画家相抗衡，始终信奉历史画乃最尊贵的艺术形式，而这恰恰也是皇家美术学院当时的院长约书亚•雷诺兹爵士一直倡导的。（The Economist）② The doctor preached about the benefits of a healthy lifestyle. 那位医生宣扬了健康生活方式的好处。
[02:47.18]additional 熟义 a. 外加的，附加的，额外的 示例 ① Family rooms start at ￡220 per night, based on two adults and one child sharing. Additional children in the room stay for free and pay for breakfast. 家庭包间每晚220英镑，可住两个大人一个孩子。有更多孩子的家庭，不额外收取住宿费，但需付早餐费。（The Guardian） ② This is the total price of your vacation—with no additional charges. 这是你度假的总费用， 无须支付额外费用。
[02:54.81]destined 熟义 a. 注定的，命中注定的；去往…的 示例 ① Dating from sixth or seventh century BC, the male forms are believed to be either the god Dionysus, or local heroes, destined to grace temples. 追溯到公元前六世纪或七世纪，男性就一直被认为或者是酒神狄奥尼索斯，或者是当地的英雄，注定要进入优雅的圣殿。（The Guardian） ② They both felt that they were destined to meet. 他们两人都觉得他们注定会见面。
[03:01.89]intrigue 熟义 vt. 激起…的兴趣，引发…的好奇心‖vi. 密谋 示例 ① The global economy is in an intriguing state, when contrasting stories about the year ahead can look equally plausible. 全球经济目前处于一个有趣的状态，与去年这个时候的情况形成鲜明对比， 但却同样似是而非。（The Economist） ② The story happened in the church intrigued her. 那个发生在教堂的故事引起了她的兴趣。
[03:08.52]deem 熟义 vt. 认为，视为 示例 ① Where the United States leads, others are following. In the European Union, up to 27% of men are considered to be obese, and almost a quarter of all children are deemed overweight. 有美国带头的地方，他国都会亦步亦趋。在欧盟国家，高达27%的男性被认为患有肥胖症，将近四分之一的儿童则被认为超重。（The Economist） ② The party was deemed a great success. 大家认为这次晚会很成功。
[03:15.91]minimise 熟义 vt. 使减少到最低限度；使显得不重要 示例 ① And this is not to minimise the tragedy and pain such a loss can generate. 而且这不是要使这种损失产生的悲剧和痛苦降到最低。（2006. 12）② I don't want to minimise their role in the campaign. 我不想贬低他们在这场运动中的作用。
[03:20.78]manipulate 熟义 vt. 操纵，控制；(熟练地)操作，使用 示例 ① There are three major design features which can be used either individually or in combination to manipulate delivery levels: filtration, paper permeability, and filter-tip ventilation. 可分别或联合应用与设计有关的三个要素，即过滤、烟卷包装纸的通透性以及过滤嘴的通气效果来控制（焦油和尼古丁的）释放水平。（The Economist） ② As a famous star, she knows how to manipulate the audience. 作为一位著名的明星，她懂得如何调动观众的情绪。
[03:29.73]scan 熟义 v. 细看；翻阅；扫描‖n. 扫描检查 示例 ① So far, Google has scanned more than 10 million titles from libraries in America and Europe—including half a million volumes held by the Bodleian in Oxford. 到目前为止，谷歌已经扫描了1000 多万本美国和欧洲的图书馆图书，其中50万本来自牛津大学波德林图书馆。（2011. 12） ② He scanned through the newspaper over dinner. 他边吃晚饭，边浏览报纸。
[03:36.80]epidemic 熟义 n. 流行病；(迅速的)泛滥，蔓延‖a. 流行的；传染性的 示例 ① If the virus had been capable of spreading through the air, or if one infected person had unknowingly entered a large population center, Ebola might have become a worldwide epidemic. 如果埃博拉病毒能够通过空气传播，或者如果一个人感染了这种病毒并在不知情的情况下进入到人口稠密的地区，那么这种病毒可能已经成为全球范围的传染病。（2013. 6）② The outbreak of a flu epidemic gives the drug store a chance to make profits. 流感的爆发给了这家药店获利的机会。
[03:46.09]bulk 熟义 n. 主体，大部分；（大）体积‖vt. 使扩大 示例 ① You were told that the rate is high because there is a "￡40m allocation and it's bulk buying". 你被告知这个比率是很高的，因为“有四千万英镑用来分配，这是一笔大买卖”。（The Guardian） ② A dozen books bulked out her bag. 里面装的十几本书把她的包撑得鼓鼓的。
[03:51.41]misfortune 熟义 n. 厄运，不幸；不幸的事故(或事件) 示例 ① All Americans, he emphasises, "want decent homes to live in; they want to locate them where they can engage in productive work; and they want some safeguard against misfortunes which cannot be wholly eliminated in this man-made world of ours." 他强调说：“所有的美国人都希望居住在体面的房子里，希望从事有成效的工作，希望有一些保护措施抵抗那些我们这个人造世界不能完全消除的厄运。”（The New York Times） ② They had the misfortune to run into a heavy sandstorm. 他们不幸遭遇了猛烈的沙尘暴。
[04:01.46]shrewd 熟义 a. 精明的，敏锐的；判断得准的，高明的 示例 ① Shrewd enough to recognise that this was the kind of agent she wanted, Myerson sent her debut novel to Coleridge and has stayed with her ever since. 迈尔森精明地意识到这就是她需要的那种代理人，于是她把她的处女作寄给了柯尔里奇，从此一直与她共事。（The Guardian） ② Bridget has a shrewd idea of what will sell. 布丽奇特很有眼光，她知道什么东西好卖。
[04:08.54]exert 熟义 vt. 运用，施加 示例 ① And yet, the same motivation that can push people to exert more effort in a constructive way could also motivate people to be more likely to engage in unethical behaviours. 然而，同样的动机可能激励人们以建设性的方式更加努力，也可能刺激人们做出不道德的事。（2012. 6）② In order to live a happy life, she would have to exert herself. 为了能够过上幸福的生活，她必须努力。
[04:15.90]withstand 熟义 vt. 承受，经受住，抵住，顶住 示例 ① That "escape velocity" refers to the strength an economy shows in which it catapults itself out of a tight range of growth and can withstand shocks such as those posed in the U.S.“逃逸速度”指的是一种经济体制在将自己弹射出一个窄幅的增长区间时所表现出的强度，这种经济体制可以经受住美国曾经遭受过的那种冲击。（CNBC）② In the Long March they had withstood siege, hunger and deprivation. 在长征中，他们经受了围攻、饥饿和物资的极度匮乏。
[04:24.53]contract 熟义 n. 合同，合约，契约 ‖v. 订立合同；缩小 示例 ① From offering classes that teach students how to legally manipulate contracts, to reinforcing the notion of profit over community interests, Etzioni has seen a lot that's left him shaking his head. 从教授学生如何合法地篡改合同到强化利润高于团体利益的观念，埃齐奥尼看到了很多令他摇头叹息的事情。（2006. 12） ② He is under contract to a major American computer firm. 他已签约一家大的美国计算机公司。
[04:32.95]probability 熟义 n. 可能性，或然性；很可能发生的事 示例 ① Can you use your mathematical knowledge to increase the probability of financial success? 你能应用数学知识增加经济成功的概率吗？（Scientific American） ② There is little probability that they will reach London tonight. 他们今晚不大可能到达伦敦。
[04:38.69]decade 熟义 n. 十年，十年期(尤指一个年代) 示例 ① Why is it even interested in all those out-of-print library books, most of which have been gathering dust on forgotten shelves for decades?（谷歌）为何会对那些不再发行的图书馆藏书感兴趣呢？它们中的大部分已经布满尘埃，被遗忘在书架上几十年了。（2011. 12）② China's economy had an increasing growth in the past decades. 在过去几十年里，中国的经济一直持续不断地增长。
[04:46.06]bare 熟义 a. 裸体的，裸露的；(树木或土地)光秃秃的 示例 ① Livers stripped bare of their original tissue then recoated with new cells have been successfully transplanted into rats for the first time. 完全剥离其原始组织然后重新用新的细胞来覆盖的肝脏已在大白鼠实验中移植成功，这在历史上尚属首次。（New Scientist） ② Every aspect of the star's private life was laid bare. 这位明星的私生活被全面曝光了。
[04:53.19]extinguish 熟义 v. 熄灭，扑灭；毁灭，消灭 示例 ① It's hard to completely extinguish bubonic plague in rodents and fleas, since there are so many of them around the world, Weinberg said. 温伯格说，“因为世界上啮齿类动物和跳蚤的数量庞大，所以要完全消灭它们带来的黑死病很困难”。（The Huffington Post）② Firefighters tried to extinguish the flames in the forest. 消防员在森林里奋力扑火。
[05:00.26]malnutrition 熟义 n. 营养不良 示例 ① Thirty years after scientists first revealed they had created the world's first GM crop, hopes that their potential to ease global malnutrition problems may be realised at last. 在科学家们第一次透露他们培植了世界上第一批转基因作物三十年后， 通过转基因作物缓解全球营养不良问题的希望最终可能会实现。（The Guardian） ② He was short because of malnutrition when he was a child. 他小时候因营养不良而身材矮小。
[05:08.37]format 熟义 n. (总体的)安排，计划，设计；(出版物的)版式，开本‖v. 格式化 示例 ① Last week Google used the still-unfinished format to let users drag files into its web-mail service. 上周，谷歌公司使用了尚未成型的设计，允许用户将文件拖拽入它们的网络邮件服务系统。（New Scientist） ② The format of the evening party has proved popular. 结果证明，那场晚会的总体安排很受欢迎。
